      "id": "c-stampede",
      "source_id": "c-stampede",
      "question": "How does Acme avoid Redis stampedes?",
      "answer": "Every key gets a TTL of 10 minutes plus random jitter of up to 60 seconds, so many keys never expire at the same moment [S1]. Acme guards hot keys with a short lock so only one request reloads it [S1].",
